Z||000003||theogre||10-02-2000||11:45 AM||||Most of the dual port 220 TBI looks plugged the same as the single port 300 TBI.<P>Judgine by what I have for notes on the ECM it should be interesting to see how he fires the second injector. By the looks of the schematics I've seen you might not be able to just hook them in parrallel. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Xtreme Fiero's||10-02-2000||05:52 PM||||Ogre: I was thinking you mught be able to hook them up in seires and raise the fuel pressure some and it would be fine.<P>anyone know when it will come out?I looked on his web site I thought that was going to be for the 2.8?<p>[This message has been edited by Xtreme Fiero's (edited 10-02-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||10-02-2000||08:31 PM||||This guy has schematics of some of the ECM's. including the 1226864 used in 85-86 L4 setups. <A HREF="http://www.cruzers.com/~ludis" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cruzers.com/~ludis</A> <P>It may be posible to do a series of the 2. My concern is that acording to the schematics on the site above the ECM has a current sense circuit in the injector control. I'm not sure just how that current sense section is used. Altering the injectors would affect that. The question is just how.<P>I was looking around westcoast earlier.... I didn't see a 4 cyl manifold in developement. Doesn't mean he's not doing one I guess. <P><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 10-02-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||rockcrawl||10-02-2000||08:48 PM||||I would think the ECM would need to be recalibrated to compensate for the increased airflow, so maybe injector current could be altered as well. Also, I believe Chris West is working on twin throttle body/port inj intake for the 2.8, not the 2.5. If mounting a dual bore TBI on a Fiero 2.5, I would think it would be more practical to use an ECM from a GM car that used a 2 barrel TBI (s-10???).<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT (awaiting new engine)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<P>"Confidence is the feeling you have before you fully understand the situation"||||reg||1
Z||000007||Cooter||10-02-2000||09:15 PM||||Why not just use the 2 bbl throttle body to begin with? We have discussed this before and it could be made to fit with a simple adapter plate- but wiring it up was the problem.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Xtreme Fiero's||10-02-2000||09:26 PM||||did any 2.5 GM cars/trucks use a 2-bbl TBI unit? I have seen them in summit for 2.8L s-10's the IAC looks the same and it has dual 2 wire injectors. what can I get a 2.5 2-bbl TBI manifold off of? what else it there to hook up but vac. lines? I am looking for a good way to really give my next 2.5/2.7 alot more air/fuel and throttle response.||||reg||1
